{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IsomorphismModule\/Matching+Graph.swift#L41","fileName":"Matching+Graph.swift"},"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P17IsomorphismModuleE12isomorphisms2toAD12IsomorphismsVyxqd__Gqd___tAaBRd__lF","title":"isomorphisms(to:)","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"IsomorphismModule"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isomorphisms","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Isomorphisms","preciseIdentifier":"s:17IsomorphismModule12IsomorphismsV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Every one of the isomorphisms from this graph onto ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"other"},{"text":": bijections between the vertices that preserve the number of edges between every ordered pair of vertices (self-loops included), as a lazy sequence; the empty graph has one, the empty mapping.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Each mapping reads from this graph to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"other"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"images"},{"text":" lists the image of each vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order. The order of the sequence is fixed for given inputs but not specified.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/isomorphismmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/isomorphisms(to:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule","doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/isomorphisms(to:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isomorphisms","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"other","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17IsomorphismModule12IsomorphismsV","text":"Isomorphisms","identifier":"doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule\/Isomorphisms","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Found by individualization–refinement. The first mapping comes from a search on both graphs at once, refined jointly after each assignment (most pairs are decided by the first refinement or a few assignments); when that search outgrows a small budget, the graphs are split into connected components and get canonical labelings by the engine of "},{"code":"automorphismGroup()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (with automorphism pruning), and the pair is isomorphic exactly when the certificates agree. The rest of the sequence is the first mapping composed with each automorphism of this graph, O(n) per mapping after the group is found. Set-up O((n + m) log n); the search is exponential in the worst case."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cancelled task ends the sequence (nil from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":"; checked every few hundred search nodes), so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isIsomorphic(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isomorphism(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" return false and nil. Wrap a call in a task with a deadline to bound it."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://IsomorphismModule/documentation/IsomorphismModule/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","title":"GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/isomorphismmodule\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule\/GraphProtocols"},"doc://IsomorphismModule/documentation/IsomorphismModule":{"kind":"symbol","title":"IsomorphismModule","url":"\/documentation\/isomorphismmodule","identifier":"doc:\/\/IsomorphismModule\/documentation\/IsomorphismModule","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IsomorphismModule/documentation/IsomorphismModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/isomorphisms(to:)":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"isomorphisms","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Other","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"ext